+// Where each prefill tensor lives in the arena. A dense layer's mixer
+// scratch (GDN or attention) dies at its output projection, before the FFN
+// writes its intermediates, and the FFN's die at its down projection, before
+// the next mixer: the three sets share one region, each packed from its
+// start, and the GDN and attention outputs (read only by their layer's FFN)
+// share another. Every dispatch of a prefill runs in one serial compute
+// encoder, so a set's writes follow the reads of the set before it.
+// Everything else (hidden rows, norms, sums, RoPE tables, captures, the
+// draft context, split scratch, MoE scratch) keeps its own range.
+struct PrefillLayout final {
+  std::array<uint64_t, prefillTensorCount> offsets{};
+  std::array<uint64_t, prefillTensorCount> sizes{};
+  uint64_t bytes = 0;
+};
